%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6538ac63e68d01d4e893f109d9378580, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialDefinition
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialDefinition
  StartingWeapon: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7991edf7f844c1b4abbdf23bd13bf5c8, type: 2}
  FirstUpgradePipes: 0
  TinkerCommonEach: 0
  MarkerRadius: 2.5
  RecoveryRadius: 48
  Pages:
  - Step: 0
    Title: WELCOME TO DUMPSTER FIRE
    Text: "Welcome to Dumpster Fire! In this survivor game, you\u2019ll face hordes
      of enemies and bosses while you improve your equipment and try to escape the
      scrapyard. Let\u2019s start with some basics."
    Controls: 0
    AdvanceWithE: 1
  - Step: 1
    Title: 01 / GET MOVING
    Text: "You can move with W/A/S/D and jump with the space bar. You can dash with
      Left Shift, which consumes a dash charge that recharges over time. If you\u2019re
      going quick enough, like after a dash, you can slide by holding Left Control.
      Walk to the highlighted area to continue."
    Controls: 1
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 2
    Title: 02 / FIRST CONTACT
    Text: An enemy has spawned! Shoot him with your left click until he dies.
    Controls: 2
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 3
    Title: 02 / COLLECT THE MATERIALS
    Text: Walk over the dropped materials to collect them.
    Controls: 1
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 4
    Title: 02 / UPGRADE YOUR AUTOCANNON
    Text: Different enemies drop different materials. You can use these materials
      to upgrade your weapons and to craft new ones. Go to the tinkering table and
      upgrade your autocannon to level 2.
    Controls: 3
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 5
    Title: 03 / FEELING THE HEAT
    Text: You are starting to attract attention! Killing enemies fills the Heat gauge,
      and the fuller it is, the more enemies will spawn. Once it reaches its maximum,
      an Overheat event will begin, spawning elite enemies and bosses.
    Controls: 0
    AdvanceWithE: 1
  - Step: 6
    Title: 03 / WEAPON ABILITIES
    Text: Luckily, you also have weapon abilities at your disposal. Each weapon has
      a unique ability, but they all consume ammo to use and have a timed cooldown.
      Press Q to use your ability to deal with this small horde.
    Controls: 4
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 7
    Title: 03 / MATERIALS FOR TINKERING
    Text: Collect the materials dropped by all three enemies, then return to the
      tinkering table.
    Controls: 1
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 8
    Title: 03 / BUILD YOUR SECOND WEAPON
    Text: With enough materials, you can Tinker at a table to create a new semi-random
      weapon. Go to the table and choose your second weapon slot to tinker a new
      weapon. If you upgrade weapons enough, you will also be able to perform Advanced
      Tinkering on them, which will evolve their capabilities or change them drastically.
    Controls: 3
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 9
    Title: 04 / YOUR WEAPONS WORK TOGETHER
    Text: "We\u2019re almost done. Your equipped weapons will cycle when you run
      out of ammo; however, unequipped weapons will still fire independently, although
      with limited range and damage. Kill the last horde of enemies with your new
      weapons to continue."
    Controls: 2
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 10
    Title: 04 / COLLECT THE LAST MATERIALS
    Text: Collect the materials from all four enemies to level up.
    Controls: 1
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 11
    Title: 04 / LEVEL UP
    Text: Apart from using them for crafting, picking materials up makes you level
      up. When you do, you will get small random stat boosts, as well as choosing
      one of three passive items. You have six item slots, differentiated by body
      parts, which can fit different items. If you already have items, you will also
      be given the choice to upgrade them up to level 6.
    Controls: 0
    AdvanceWithE: 0
  - Step: 12
    Title: 04 / YOUR WAY OUT
    Text: Your goal is to leave the scrapyard. To do this, you need to trigger enough
      Overheat cycles to attract the two bosses, collect their core batteries and
      use them to power a massive gate found somewhere between the trash piles.
    Controls: 0
    AdvanceWithE: 1
  - Step: 13
    Title: 04 / TAKE TO THE SKY
    Text: "To finish the tutorial, walk towards the trash geyser. It will make you
      jump up to the floating islands in the sky. These are ripe with opportunities,
      as well as being the only place you\u2019ll find tinkering stations. Be warned,
      however, that during Overheat events, you will be forced to jump back down
      to the scrapyard."
    Controls: 1
    AdvanceWithE: 0
